// Nursery — the capability passed to a function that needs to spawn into its
// caller's nursery (the Trio escape hatch). See ASYNC.md, "Escape hatch:
// passing the nursery".
//
// A Nursery is a lightweight wrapper around the per-invocation tracking state
// of an `async { }` block: a pointer to the futures array and a pointer to
// the count slot. Both live on the async block's stack frame, so a Nursery
// value is only valid for the lifetime of its enclosing `async` block (which
// is exactly the structured-concurrency invariant — the block cannot exit
// until every spawned task, including those spawned through a passed Nursery,
// has finished).
//
// `nursery.spawn(fn, args...)` is special-cased by the compiler (it needs the
// spawn trampoline machinery), so it is NOT a regular method declared here.
// The two fields are the full runtime contract.

pub struct Nursery : Sendable {
	pub var uint64 futures_ptr = 0
	pub var uint64 count_ptr = 0
}
